  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Boston's Jake Bennett carries a 2.90 ERA into tonight's rematch, and the Athletics' lineup is searching for life after totaling 16 strikeouts across 2 hits yesterday. The question is not whether they can score. It's whether they can score before falling behind by five again.",
    "what_this_means": "The second inning decided this game. Jack Perkins lasted three innings, gave up five runs on five hits, and the Athletics never recovered. This is what happens when a starter exits early in a blowout: the bullpen inherits a crater, not a game to hold. Soderstrom hit a solo shot to cut it to 11-1, but one run off Boston's pitching staff was not a narrative. It was a courtesy. The pattern of inconsistency did not show a new shape yesterday. The team that scores once does not win, and yesterday proved it does not even come close. Sixteen strikeouts is not a slump. It is surrender.",
    "what_to_watch": "Boston again, same field, different starter. Bennett has been sharp, so execution matters from the first pitch.",
